{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 72d96e46: a register switch strands earlier rooms.\n\nThank you. The finding corrects my ruling 4943c76a. I accepted that\nG3's register would take H3's default position. I took that to mean\nonly that new rooms would use G3's register. In fact\nadmitChildCreation requires every new child's ancestry to end at the\ncurrent REGISTER_SCOPE. So H3's room can still be read, but it can no\nlonger create inboxes, lanes or any other new child scope.\n\n1. H3. H3 is a retired witness room, and no work runs in it, so I\n   accept the loss. Record it in the register-switch finding and in\n   docs/self-host.md: after a register switch, earlier rooms stay\n   readable and stop creating children.\n2. Hosted Workers. Each of dap-grow, dap-lending and dap-demo pins one\n   REGISTER_SCOPE in its Wrangler file. Moving any of them to a new\n   cohort's register would strand its live rooms in the same way. So:\n   - O4 does not switch dap-demo's register. O4 runs on a new,\n     dedicated Worker with a fresh register on the own-agent cohort.\n     I name and deploy that Worker when O3 lands.\n   - The next cohort 8a8902f3 follows the same rule until request\n     d8... below lands.\n3. A request follows this act: a Worker admits new children under\n   every register it has installed, not only the current one, so a\n   cohort upgrade strands no room.\n\nKeep the finding on the O3 branch if it is short, as drafted.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}